      },
      "text": "INCREMENTAL ENCODER:\n+------------------+\n| Counts pulses as |\n| disk rotates.    |\n| Requires homing  |\n| after power-on.  |\n+------------------+\n Loses count on power cycle. Homing routine on startup.\n Cheaper. Most industrial servos use this."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SENSORS.md#010",
      "path": [
        "03-SENSORS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:robotics:03-sensors, git-history:robotics:03-sensors]",
        "canonical_path": "robotics/03-SENSORS.md",
        "concepts": "[sensors]",
        "current_path": "robotics/03-SENSORS.md",
        "id": "maxim:robotics:sensors",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "robotics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[sensors]",
        "section": "robotics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Robotics - Sensors",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ABSOLUTE ENCODER:\n+------------------+\n| Outputs absolute |\n| angle (Gray code |\n| or SSI/BiSS      |\n| protocol).       |\n+------------------+\n Retains position through power cycle. No homing needed.\n More expensive. Surgical robots, cobots."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SENSORS.md#011",
      "path": [
        "03-SENSORS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:robotics:03-sensors, git-history:robotics:03-sensors]",
